; regression test for a real bug: a labelled conjunction claim (split into per-conjunct
; derivation steps, then combined via "and-intro") used to silently lose its label. The
; per-conjunct loop in `eval_expression` reused the same `label` variable the *combined*
; formula needed later, resetting it to `''` -- so `P and R "derived-conjunction"` was always
; stored unlabelled, regardless of what was written. Confirmed via `P` (only ever established
; through an unlabelled bare `use P`, so it's only exported at all because the labelled
; conjunction needs it as a free symbol) and `R` (same story) both surviving.
load load-export-bare-claim-helper
expect "EvalError"
    bool P
expect "EvalError"
    bool R
true
;;; Proof checked.
